cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Verifiable mechanistic interpretability by grading explanations using simulations"
abstract: >-
  An explanation of a trained modular-addition transformer is graded by having a weights-blind LLM agent (Claude
  Haiku 5.5 in Claude Code, sandboxed with no network except its model endpoint) rebuild the network's weights from
  the explanation alone, then comparing the replacement with the original
  by output KL divergence and symmetry-aware hidden-state similarity. Developed in a mechanistic interpretability
  hackathon on automatically evaluating mechanistic interpretability explanations, co-organized by the authors in
  their mechanistic interpretability community (https://mechinterp.com/).
authors:
